{"parentUuid":"4dce167f-b509-4ed3-b07a-fdf80d261d58","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"3972e979-5e75-4953-aa06-0c7c970352c1","agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CL6kxquZ5395bsx8QMuUYG","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Baylor Offensive Play-Call Analysis\n3:## 2024 and 2025, 1,935 charted plays across 25 games\n9:## The headline\n24:## Where it broke\n28:### 1. First down\n34:### 2. The run game\n48:### 3. Early-down running\n61:### 4. The offense stopped running\n70:## How much to trust this\n85:## A labelling change you need to know about\n102:## Where the offense won and lost\n105:### Down and distance\n130:### Play type\n152:### Run concept\n169:### Pass concept\n187:### Formation family\n207:### Personnel\n218:### Field zone\n231:### Quarter\n245:### Quarterback\n254:### Opponent\n284:### Early downs (1st and 2nd)\n293:### Two-minute (last 2:00 of either half)\n302:### Early-down play type\n324:## Against the defence\n329:### Dropback success by coverage\n342:### Dropback success by pressure\n351:### Dropback success by blitz\n360:### Dropback success by rusher count\n375:### Run success by defensive personnel\n388:### Success by box count\n405:### Success by charted defensive personnel\n421:### 2024 only — success by charted front\n435:### 2024 only — success by charted coverage family\n450:## Both seasons pooled\n454:### concept\n466:### coverage\n477:### def package\n488:### down distance\n505:### field zone\n514:### formation\n532:### pass concept\n557:### personnel\n566:### play type\n584:### quarter\n595:### run pass\n604:## Coordinator tendency profile\n608:### down / distance / personnel\n630:### down / distance / play / type\n667:### down / distance / run / pass\n701:### field / zone / personnel\n717:### field / zone / play / type\n754:### field / zone / run / pass\n775:### quarter / personnel\n792:### quarter / play / type\n829:### quarter / run / pass\n852:## What this cannot answer\n