{"parentUuid":"1074d13e-4c69-49c2-b73e-35cf1346e807","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceu3m8EP3vP2HEPNzkLSj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KfgPmhj2e8CE8C3zU9wjm1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":".venv/bin/python -m pytest -q 2>&1 | tail -3 && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git log --oneline -1\nLoad PFF alignment fields and assemble the alignment play table\n\nPhase 4 builds on outputs/joined_plays_enriched.parquet rather than redoing\nthe Phase 1 join, but that parquet predates the charting widening, so the new\nchart columns have to be re-attached on (season, game_code, play_no).\n\nBoth attach steps are asserted rather than trusted, because both failure modes\nhere are silent. A many-to-one chart merge would inflate every denominator\ndownstream and the success rates would still look plausible, so the key\nuniqueness, the row count and the unmatched count are all checked and the\nmerge is declared one_to_one. The PFF attach goes through analysis._play_key\nbecause play_id is float64 and a naive .astype(str) matches zero rows without\nraising anything.\n\nThat last one is pinned as a test that asserts the naive join matches exactly\nzero rows, so the trap has a tripwire rather than a comment. The team_play\noffense filter has one too: team_play carries both teams and they share\nplay_id values, so without the filter the opponent's alignment would merge\nonto Baylor's plays.\n\nOverlapping PFF columns are suffixed _pff rather than overwriting the Phase 1\nvalues, which keeps a source disagreement visible instead of resolving it by\naccident.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cpiq4uQvzv6fct94zkaVCX\nEOF","description":"Run suite and commit Tasks 2-3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2700,"cache_read_input_tokens":163388,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2700,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ceu3m6mpiMLvyw3DRzrye","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"superpowers:using-git-worktrees","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"f239d27c-f9d0-410b-8dc4-ad9269915261","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:28:13.626Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.worktrees/phase4-alignment","sessionId":"b8143861-beec-4930-9c27-06bc9d94fa8b","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"main"}
