{"parentUuid":"9511726a-14cb-4b70-8ae9-994147bbe6b9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceu3rLcAeZk5Qiz74SrTp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019qN1zRFhmoDbYm3dVuMxbd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":".venv/bin/python -m pytest -q 2>&1 | tail -3 && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git log --oneline -1\nNormalise the drifted alignment vocabularies and derive the dimensions\n\nEvery chart column with a vocabulary moved between the two seasons. Personnel\nwent from 4 labels to 11 because 2025 subdivides twelve personnel into\n12S/12B/12W/12M/12P/12J; Form Fam writes UNBALANCED in 2024 and UNBAL in 2025.\nGrouped raw, a pure relabelling would land in the mix term and be read as\n\"Baylor lined up differently\" — which is exactly the false positive this phase\nis built to detect, so the normalisers are the load-bearing part of it.\n\nThey are mechanical rather than hand-mapped, and their output is published as\na crosswalk with counts so the mapping can be checked rather than believed.\n\ndecode_offense_package refuses to invent a personnel code for a package that\nis short a player. A \"(*)\" suffix means PFF could not place that many players\nand \"(+Q)\" means a second quarterback took a skill slot; neither has an honest\nRB-TE reading, so both become OTHER with a recorded note. Shipping a guessed\nvalue would have been the easy path and is the thing the task forbade.\n\n_binary_from_pff exists because PFF writes motion and option as 1.0-or-null\nwith no explicit zero. Averaging the non-nulls would report a 100% motion rate\non every cut, and nothing would error. That has its own test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cpiq4uQvzv6fct94zkaVCX\nEOF","description":"Run suite and commit Task 4"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","st