{"parentUuid":"308ff7ff-f537-4aaa-adcd-a91221b43109","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14804330 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e0e63622-0677-4728-b5bf-b28861705ea4","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:32:15.545Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14804330 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.worktrees/phase4-alignment","sessionId":"b8143861-beec-4930-9c27-06bc9d94fa8b","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"e0e63622-0677-4728-b5bf-b28861705ea4","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceu45jGHnA8cgh5vu9twb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L9NARXG2qXj848kNAjYW4m","name":"Bash","input":{"command":".venv/bin/python -m pytest -q 2>&1 | tail -3 && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git log --oneline -1\nRegenerate the evidence for both resolved PFF fields as tables\n\nThe spec resolves two undocumented PFF fields by argument. These functions\nturn that argument into output a reader can check.\n\nmofo_resolution recomputes the split the whole defensive-look section rests\non: character 2 agrees with Baylor's own 2024 charted coverage family far more\nstrongly than character 1 does, so character 2 is the played coverage and\ncharacter 1 is the pre-snap shown look. It also emits the corroborating\nasymmetry - defences show open and rotate closed far more often than the\nreverse - because a single agreement rate is one line of evidence and two\nindependent ones are worth more than a stronger claim on one.\n\nIts test pins both rates. The point is not that the numbers are pretty; it is\nthat a PFF re-ingest that changed the field's encoding would otherwise flip\nthe meaning of every defensive table without failing anything.\n\ncolumn_audit measures fill on every run and only takes the verdict text from a\nconstant. A fill rate typed into a table by hand is exactly the kind of figure\nthat is right the day it is written and wrong three months later with nothing\nto catch it.\n\nsource_agreement checks the places where the chart and PFF both carry a field.\nThe def_package row is load-bearing: it shows the team_play feed matches the\nrushing feed on every overlapping row, which is what makes it safe to use\nteam_play for all plays instead of pooling a dropbacks-only field with a\nruns-only one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cpiq4uQvzv6fct94zkaVCX\nEOF","description":"Run suite and commit Task 7"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4593,"cache_read_input_tokens":187578,"output_tokens":693,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4593},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":693,"cache_read_input_tokens":187578,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4593,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ceu45hqU8UZMXuDazQwSs","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"superpowers:using-git-worktrees","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"2407ecf6-d649-4d78-94ac-110ef0d0ea9a","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:32:28.073Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.worktrees/phase4-alignment","sessionId":"b8143861-beec-4930-9c27-06bc9d94fa8b","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"main"}
