{"parentUuid":"c29f008f-3b09-49e9-b740-d9fffe76515c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceu4RVEzsgznqwvYTUhas","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AY6Yamux4JMPssVyQKupY5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git diff main --stat | tail -20\nRender outputs/ALIGNMENT.md, with the null result stated in the first paragraph\n\nThe answer is a null result on the mix hypothesis, so the report says so\nplainly and early rather than hunting for a flattering slice. Across every\ndimension tested the largest mix term is about a point against a typical\nefficacy term of eight; Baylor did not line up meaningfully differently and\ndefences did not line up meaningfully differently against them.\n\nThe renderer computes nothing. It formats numerals out of the summary table\nand the provenance JSON, and the tests that matter are the ones that change a\ntable value and assert the prose changes with it - including the negative\ncase, where the null-result sentence must disappear once the mix term\ndominates. A report that always says \"does not explain\" is not reporting a\nnull result, it is asserting one.\n\nThe honesty section goes before the findings rather than after them. It states\nthe sample sizes, the roughly fifteen-point interval on a forty-play cell, and\nthat cells are sorted by size and never ranked by change.\n\nThe formation-by-concept table is printed even though every cell is below the\nfloor, because the fragmentation is the honest answer to \"did the same call\nfrom the same look stop working\" - the data cannot resolve it at that\ngranularity, and saying so is better than picking the least-thin cell.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cpiq4uQvzv6fct94zkaVCX\nEOF","description":"Commit report and check diff against main"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3873,"cache_read_input_tokens":219689,"output_tokens":681,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":76},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3873},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":681,"cache_read_input_tokens":219689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3873,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ceu4RUJBceQrErf8CuJWf","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"superpowers:using-git-worktrees","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"9c33e694-02ee-4cb9-831d-d51f380bb716","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:36:55.899Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.worktrees/phase4-alignment","sessionId":"b8143861-beec-4930-9c27-06bc9d94fa8b","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"main"}
