{"parentUuid":"950945f9-287b-49bc-bff6-4197b429cc3c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceu4U4gxkXh8U7gj9pV1W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GU4tRxWx7v1eu371NhGEBh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n \"99.0%\\|98.6%\\|54.3%\\|40.3%\\| 67\\b\" outputs/ALIGNMENT.md | grep -v '^\\s*[0-9]*:|' | head","description":"Locate remaining hardcoded figures in the report"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":652,"cache_read_input_tokens":227361,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":652,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ceu4U3ktjkT3Yg5apXPQh","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"superpowers:using-git-worktrees","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"04c74403-608d-4d83-a484-727b70f59da3","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:37:31.166Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.worktrees/phase4-alignment","sessionId":"b8143861-beec-4930-9c27-06bc9d94fa8b","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"04c74403-608d-4d83-a484-727b70f59da3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"3972e979-5e75-4953-aa06-0c7c970352c1","agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GU4tRxWx7v1eu371NhGEBh","type":"tool_result","content":"111:This is where *same look, same call, less output* would show if it could be measured. It cannot: **67 of 67 cells fall below the 30-play floor in at least one season**. The table is printed because the fragmentation is itself the answer, not so that a cell can be picked out of it.\n203:**`offense_package`** is undocumented upstream — PFF's own schema declares it as a bare string. It is a four-slot count, **WR-FB-RB-TE**, over the five non-OL, non-QB players on the field. `3-0-1-1` is 11 personnel, on 1,743 plays. It agrees with the chart's own `Personnel` column on 99.0% of joined plays, and the chart column is used in preference because it is fully populated and `offense_package` is not.\n205:**`mofo_coverage_played_shown`** reads *shown then played*, which is the reverse of the word order in its own name. Its second character agrees with Baylor's 2024 charted coverage family on 91.8% of 826 plays; the first agrees on only 67.1%. Coaches chart the coverage that was played, so the second character is the played look and the first is the pre-snap show. Independently, defences show open and rotate closed 419 times against 156 the other way, which is the asymmetry that reading predicts. The evidence follows the data rather than the label.\n215:- **Whether the tight-end alignment fill drop is real.** `pff_TEALIGNMENT` fell from 54.3% filled to 40.3%, and this data cannot say whether fewer tight ends aligned attached or fewer were charted. It is excluded from the decomposition for that reason and blank is treated as its own category everywhere else.\n228:Every figure above is read from those tables or from `outputs/alignment_provenance.json` at render time. 98.6% of charted plays carry PFF alignment fields.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4ee8d891-c43f-4cf1-9bd0-9cde92f8d92e","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:37:31.351Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"111:This is where *same look, same call, less output* would show if it could be measured. It cannot: **67 of 67 cells fall below the 30-play floor in at least one season**. The table is printed because the fragmentation is itself the answer, not so that a cell can be picked out of it.\n203:**`offense_package`** is undocumented upstream — PFF's own schema declares it as a bare string. It is a four-slot count, **WR-FB-RB-TE**, over the five non-OL, non-QB players on the field. `3-0-1-1` is 11 personnel, on 1,743 plays. It agrees with the chart's own `Personnel` column on 99.0% of joined plays, and the chart column is used in preference because it is fully populated and `offense_package` is not.\n205:**`mofo_coverage_played_shown`** reads *shown then played*, which is the reverse of the word order in its own name. Its second character agrees with Baylor's 2024 charted coverage family on 91.8% of 826 plays; the first agrees on only 67.1%. Coaches chart the coverage that was played, so the second character is the played look and the first is the pre-snap show. Independently, defences show open and rotate closed 419 times against 156 the other way, which is the asymmetry that reading predicts. The evidence follows the data rather than the label.\n215:- **Whether the tight-end alignment fill drop is real.** `pff_TEALIGNMENT` fell from 54.3% filled to 40.3%, and this data cannot say whether fewer tight ends aligned attached or fewer were charted. It is excluded from the decomposition for that reason and blank is treated as its own category everywhere else.\n228:Every figure above is read from those tables or from `outputs/alignment_provenance.json` at render time. 98.6% of charted plays carry PFF alignment fields.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"04c74403-60