{"parentUuid":"d5151c48-c65d-49ec-84d6-3c5f9b951b60","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceu4aAnjXDWDUQvbvPxUq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TDPAZeEV4BiE3YpvjYBGZx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":".venv/bin/python build_alignment_tables.py >/dev/null && .venv/bin/python build_alignment_report.py && echo \"=== exclusion section ===\" && sed -n '/## What could not be built/,/^## Two PFF/p' outputs/ALIGNMENT.md && echo \"=== TE bullet ===\" && grep -n \"pff_TEALIGNMENT\" outputs/ALIGNMENT.md | tail -1","description":"Rebuild and inspect the corrected sections"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":234814,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":344,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ceu4a9ohHtRGUzoQ4zCUz","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"superpowers:using-git-worktrees","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"b784c0a9-602e-4102-9ae9-b1191748d7c7","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:38:44.607Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.worktrees/phase4-alignment","sessionId":"b8143861-beec-4930-9c27-06bc9d94fa8b","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b784c0a9-602e-4102-9ae9-b1191748d7c7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"3972e979-5e75-4953-aa06-0c7c970352c1","agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TDPAZeEV4BiE3YpvjYBGZx","type":"tool_result","content":"wrote outputs/ALIGNMENT.md\n=== exclusion section ===\n## What could not be built, and why\n\nA reader who expects a front-versus-outcome table needs to be told it cannot exist, not left to assume it was overlooked.\n\n- **`RB Align`** — 89.9% filled in 2024 and 0.0% in 2025. Well charted in 2024 and not charted at all in 2025.\n- **`Front`** — 98.3% filled in 2024 and 0.0% in 2025. Well charted in 2024 and not charted at all in 2025.\n- **`Cover Family`** — 90.0% filled in 2024 and 0.4% in 2025. Well charted in 2024 and effectively absent in 2025; its 2024 values are what resolved the mofo field.\n- **`Front Adjust`** — 32.2% filled in 2024 and 9.5% in 2025. Fill collapsed and the vocabulary changed.\n- **`Stunt`** — 12.7% filled in 2024 and 11.4% in 2025. 2025 collapsed to a bare y on almost every charted row, so the label carries no information.\n- **`Shifts`** — 2.5% filled in 2024 and 2.2% in 2025. Too rare in the chart; pff shift is used instead.\n- **`Hash_O`** — 0.0% filled in 2024 and 0.2% in 2025. Empty in both seasons; pff ball_snapped_from replaces it.\n- **`shotgun`** — 99.4% filled in 2024 and 97.8% in 2025. Near-constant; a constant explains nothing.\n- **`no_huddle`** — 99.4% filled in 2024 and 97.8% in 2025. Zero positives in either season.\n\n---\n\n## Two PFF fields this phase had to resolve first\n=== TE bullet ===\n215:- **Whether the tight-end alignment fill drop is real.** `pff_TEALIGNMENT` fell from 54.4% filled to 40.3%, and this data cannot say whether fewer tight ends aligned attached or fewer were charted. It is excluded from the decomposition for that reason and blank is treated as its own category everywhere else.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ebd60ac3-3335-4925-bd98-22b77097ec72","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:38:45.980Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"wrote outputs/ALIGNMENT.md\n=== exclusion section ===\n## What could not be built, and why\n\nA reader who expects a front-versus-outcome table needs to be told it cannot exist, not left to assume it was overlooked.\n\n- **`RB Align`** — 89.9% filled in 2024 and 0.0% in 2025. Well charted in 2024 and not charted at all in 2025.\n- **`Front`** — 98.3% filled in 2024 and 0.0% in 2025. Well charted in 2024 and not charted at all in 2025.\n- **`Cover Family`** — 90.0% filled in 2024 and 0.4% in 2025. Well charted in 2024 and effectively absent in 2025; its 2024 values are what resolved the mofo field.\n- **`Front Adjust`** — 32.2% filled in 2024 and 9.5% in 2025. Fill collapsed and the vocabulary changed.\n- **`Stunt`** — 12.7% filled in 2024 and 11.4% in 2025. 2025 collapsed to a bare y on almost every charted row, so the label carries no information.\n- **`Shifts`** — 2.5% filled in 2024 and 2.2% in 2025. Too rare in the chart; pff shift is used instead.\n- **`Hash_O`** — 0.0% filled in 2024 and 0.2% in 2025. Empty in both seasons; pff ball_snapped_from replaces it.\n- **`shotgun`** — 99.4% filled in 2024 and 97.8% in 2025. Near-constant; a constant explains nothing.\n- **`no_huddle`** — 99.4% filled in 2024 and 97.8% in 2025. Zero positives in either season.\n\n---\n\n## Two PFF fields this phase had to resolve first\n=== TE bullet ===\n215:- **Whether the tight-end alignment fill drop is real.** `pff_TEALIGNMENT` fell from 54.4% filled to 40.3%, and this data cannot say whether fewer tight ends aligned attached or fewer were charted. It is excluded from the decomposition for that reason and blank is treated as its own category everywhere else.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b784c0a9-602e-4102-9ae9-b1191748d7c7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.wo