{"parentUuid":"f14a46b7-a2d6-4b92-b218-d738cfc27651","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceu51kKYuQWeNEgTKvZeo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013gUn1KzkcotagqNPTtpaUd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n '/^### Explosive rate/,/^---/p' outputs/ALIGNMENT.md; echo \"=== mofo para ===\"; grep -n \"mofo_coverage_played_shown\" outputs/ALIGNMENT.md | head -1 | cut -d: -f1 | xargs -I{} sed -n '{}p' outputs/ALIGNMENT.md; echo; echo \"=== pff exclusion lines ===\"; grep -n \"shotgun\\`\\|no_huddle\\`\" outputs/ALIGNMENT.md\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Inspect explosive section, mofo paragraph, exclusion wording"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1741,"cache_read_input_tokens":255908,"output_tokens":300,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1741},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":300,"cache_read_input_tokens":255908,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1741,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1741,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ceu51jM1JVDkzrWMNsU9a","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"superpowers:using-git-worktrees","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"fedf3a11-2c43-474c-9c4f-58b3ba2ee534","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:44:32.309Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.worktrees/phase4-alignment","sessionId":"b8143861-beec-4930-9c27-06bc9d94fa8b","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"fedf3a11-2c43-474c-9c4f-58b3ba2ee534","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"3972e979-5e75-4953-aa06-0c7c970352c1","agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013gUn1KzkcotagqNPTtpaUd","type":"tool_result","content":"### Explosive rate\n\nPhase 1 found the explosive-play rate roughly halved, from 14.8% to 7.4%. Run through the identical decomposition, the largest combined weights effect on any dimension is -0.4 points, on `form_fam_norm`, against a total change of -7.4 points. The explosive collapse is the same story as the success-rate collapse: not a mix effect.\n\n---\n=== mofo para ===\n**`mofo_coverage_played_shown`** reads *shown then played*, which is the reverse of the word order in its own name. Its second character agrees with Baylor's 2024 charted coverage family on 91.8% of 826 plays; the first agrees on only 67.1%. Coaches chart the coverage that was played, so the second character is the played look and the first is the pre-snap show — an **assumption**, and the hinge of the whole reading: if coaches charted the pre-snap shell instead, the same agreement would mean the field's own word order was right after all. Independently, defences show open and rotate closed 419 times against 156 the other way, which is the asymmetry that reading predicts. The evidence follows the data rather than the label.\n\n=== pff exclusion lines ===\n202:- **`shotgun`** — 99.4% present in 2024 and 97.8% in 2025. Near-constant; a constant explains nothing.\n203:- **`no_huddle`** — 99.4% present in 2024 and 97.8% in 2025. Zero positives in either season.\n........................................................................ [ 96%]\n.....                                                                    [100%]\n149 passed in 6.72s","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8c742842-3d4d-47cf-ab99-406bb5279340","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:44:39.388Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"### Explosive rate\n\nPhase 1 found the explosive-play rate roughly halved, from 14.8% to 7.4%. Run through the identical decomposition, the largest combined weights effect on any dimension is -0.4 points, on `form_fam_norm`, against a total change of -7.4 points. The explosive collapse is the same story as the success-rate collapse: not a mix effect.\n\n---\n=== mofo para ===\n**`mofo_coverage_played_shown`** reads *shown then played*, which is the reverse of the word order in its own name. Its second character agrees with Baylor's 2024 charted coverage family on 91.8% of 826 plays; the first agrees on only 67.1%. Coaches chart the coverage that was played, so the second character is the played look and the first is the pre-snap show — an **assumption**, and the hinge of the whole reading: if coaches charted the pre-snap shell instead, the same agreement would mean the field's own word order was right after all. Independently, defences show open and rotate closed 419 times against 156 the other way, which is the asymmetry that reading predicts. The evidence follows the data rather than the label.\n\n=== pff exclusion lines ===\n202:- **`shotgun`** — 99.4% present in 2024 and 97.8% in 2025. Near-constant; a constant explains nothing.\n203:- **`no_huddle`** — 99.4% present in 2024 and 97.8% in 2025. Zero positives in either season.\n........................................................................ [ 96%]\n.....                                                                    [100%]\n149 passed in 6.72s","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fedf3a11-2c43-474c-9c4f-58b3ba2ee534","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.worktrees/phase4-alignment","sessionId":"b8143861-beec-4930-9c27-06bc9d94fa8b","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8c742842-3d4d-47cf-ab99-406bb5279340","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14502502 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"33335f99-00f6-47c9-83ff-21a628d4779d","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:44:39.392Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14502502 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.worktrees/phase4-alignment","sessionId":"b8143861-beec-4930-9c27-06bc9d94fa8b","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"33335f99-00f6-47c9-83ff-21a628d4779d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceu52ZQjzATeaDjwyKhT6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015CqmPXdVbsuUGgoCxQNxnB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git log --oneline -1\nGuard the verdict on the effect it actually claims, and cover explosive rate\n\nThree corrections found in verification review, none of which moves the\nanswer.\n\nThe verdict sentence says \"hold 2025 usage at its 2024 level and the season\nlooks the same\". That counterfactual is sum (p1-p0)*r1, which expands to mix\nPLUS interaction - but the negligibility guard tested |mix| alone. On this\ndata both are small (largest combined weights effect 1.4 points on\ndef_package_norm against an eight-point efficacy term) so the null result\nstands, but the guard was not guarding the sentence it sits above, and a tiny\nmix with a large interaction is entirely reachable once Phase 2's EPA replaces\nsuccess rate. The guard now takes the larger of the two, the prose reports\nboth, and a test drives mix to zero with a large interaction and asserts the\nnull-result sentence disappears.\n\nThe mofo reading rests on coaches charting the coverage that was played rather\nthan the one shown. That is well founded - the Cover Family values are\npost-snap families - but it is an assumption and it is the hinge: were it\nwrong, the same 91.8% agreement would mean the field's own word order was\nright. It is now marked as an assumption in both the spec and the report,\nalongside the fullback slot which already was.\n\nExplosive rate was in scope, decomposed, written to a table and then never\nrendered - despite Phase 1 leading with it halving. It gets a paragraph, read\nfrom that table. Its largest weights effect is -0.4 points against a -7.4\npoint total, so the explosive collapse is the same story as the success-rate\ncollapse.\n\nAlso: a PFF boolean that is \"99.4% filled\" with \"zero positives\" reads as a\ncontradiction. For those rows the word is now \"present\", since a recorded\nfalse is not a missing value.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cpiq4uQvzv6fct94zkaVCX\nEOF","description":"Commit the three verification corrections"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":844,"cache_read_input_tokens":257649,"output_tokens":781,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":844},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":781,"cache_read_input_tokens":257649,"cache_creation_input_tokens":844,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":844,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ceu52YCKKYwX6bMh9RoWy","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"superpowers:using-git-worktrees","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"54380215-77b9-40cf-8117-6f81f6ddf7fb","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:44:52.051Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.worktrees/phase4-alignment","sessionId":"b8143861-beec-4930-9c27-06bc9d94fa8b","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"main"}
