{"parentUuid":"6c63f72f-7503-44bd-9820-894fc5172569","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"3972e979-5e75-4953-aa06-0c7c970352c1","agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FdFhY1XiXDcb1ZTNCDYC1J","type":"tool_result","content":"=== FINAL: fresh suite ===\n........................................................................ [ 96%]\n.....                                                                    [100%]\n149 passed in 7.21s\n\n=== modified vs main ===\nsrc/playcalls/charting.py\n\n=== tree clean? ===\n(blank = clean)\n\n=== branch / commits ===\nphase4-alignment\n      12\n\n=== deliverables ===\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 kristinarash  staff   2635 Sep  9 22:44 outputs/alignment_provenance.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 kristinarash  staff  26072 Sep  9 22:44 outputs/ALIGNMENT.md\n      99","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c243e992-3225-41dc-9efd-ee2a11b4ef75","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:45:03.453Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== FINAL: fresh suite ===\n........................................................................ [ 96%]\n.....                                                                    [100%]\n149 passed in 7.21s\n\n=== modified vs main ===\nsrc/playcalls/charting.py\n\n=== tree clean? ===\n(blank = clean)\n\n=== branch / commits ===\nphase4-alignment\n      12\n\n=== deliverables ===\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 kristinarash  staff   2635 Sep  9 22:44 outputs/alignment_provenance.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 kristinarash  staff  26072 Sep  9 22:44 outputs/ALIGNMENT.md\n      99","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6c63f72f-7503-44bd-9820-894fc5172569","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.worktrees/phase4-alignment","sessionId":"b8143861-beec-4930-9c27-06bc9d94fa8b","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c243e992-3225-41dc-9efd-ee2a11b4ef75","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14502502 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a0826af0-d468-4e0d-8e5a-7ca2788a5f43","timestamp":"2026-09-10T03:45:03.456Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14502502 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/.worktrees/phase4-alignment","sessionId":"b8143861-beec-4930-9c27-06bc9d94fa8b","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"a0826af0-d468-4e0d-8e5a-7ca2788a5f43","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5c3145ddf1f0dffe","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceu54Kqj1ZSqd4Fx26mG4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verified: 149 tests pass (76 pre-existing + 73 new), `charting.py` is the only modified file, tree clean, 12 commits on `phase4-alignment`.\n\n## Phase 4 report\n\n### 1. What `offense_package` means\n\n**`WR - FB - RB - TE`, counting the five non-OL, non-QB players.** Evidence, all reproducible in `outputs/tables/alignment_offense_package_crosswalk.csv`:\n\n- PFF's own swagger (`PFF_Data_Project/docs/swagger/premium-feeds.yaml:1942`) declares it `type: string` with no description. No data dictionary exists there — it had to be derived.\n- Across all 4,517 `team_play` rows league-wide the four slots sum to 5 on 3,628 of 3,755 parseable rows, and `offense_players` holds exactly 11 jerseys on all 1,907 joined Baylor plays. 11 − 5 OL − 1 QB = 5.\n- Cross-tab against the chart's `Personnel`: `3-0-1-1`→`11` (1,743/1,749), `2-0-1-2`→`12` (106/110), `4-0-1-0`→`10` (30/30), `1-0-1-3`→`13` (7/7). `13` putting its 3 in slot 4 rules out slot 2 being TE; `10` fixes WR and TE; the remaining 1 is the back.\n- Suffixes: every `(*)`-value sums to <5 with the deficit equal to the asterisk count → unidentified players. `(+Q)` = a second QB in a skill slot. `X-X-X-X` = unidentified.\n- **Slot 2 = FB is an ASSUMPTION**, marked as such: max 1, non-zero on 60 of 3,755 league rows and **1 of 2,311 Baylor snaps**. Immaterial here.\n\nI did **not** ship it as a grouping dimension. Chart `Personnel` is 100% filled vs 97.8% and the two agree on 99.0%, so `Personnel` is primary and `offense_package` is a cross-check.\n\n**Bonus resolution:** `mofo_coverage_played_shown` reads **shown-then-played — the reverse of its own name**. Char 2 agrees with Baylor's 2024 charted `Cover Family` on 91.8% of 826 plays; char 1 on only 67.1%. Corroborated by defences showing open and rotating closed 419 times vs 156 the other way. This rests on an assumption (coaches chart the played coverage), marked as such in spec §4.1 and in the report.\n\n### 2. Does alignment explain the decline? **No — it is an efficacy drop, not a mix shift.**\n\nOverall −7.9 points: **mix −0.5, efficacy −8.8, interaction +1.3.** Across all 13 dimensions the largest mix term anywhere is 1.1 points (`mofo_shown`) and the largest mix+interaction is 1.4 points (`def_package_norm`), against a typical efficacy term of 8.0.\n\nThe best-powered cut, **early-down runs by concept** — all 5 groups clear n≥30 in both seasons: **mix −0.8, efficacy −18.0** on a −19.0 total. Every concept fell: Inside Zone 66.7→49.5 (156/107), Counter 62.2→38.5 (74/65), Man 59.1→38.9 (44/54), Outside Zone 53.3→30.0 (30/30).\n\nExplosive rate is the same story: largest weights effect −0.4 against a −7.4 total.\n\nBaylor lined up the same way, defences lined up the same way against them, and the same concepts produced less.\n\n### 3. Three most interesting tables\n\n- `outputs/tables/alignment_decomposition_summary.csv` — 58 rows, every dimension × subset, mix/efficacy/interaction summing exactly to delta\n- `outputs/tables/alignment_decomposition_run_concept_early_down_runs.csv` — the only cut where every group clears the low-n floor\n- `outputs/tables/alignment_mofo_resolution.csv` — the evidence that inverts the field's name\n\nReport: `outputs/ALIGNMENT.md`. Spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-09-playcalls-phase4-alignment-design.md`.\n\n### 4. What I could not determine\n\n- **Why efficacy fell.** Not measurable here.\n- **Front / coverage-family effects.** Baylor stopped charting them: `Front` 98.3%→0.0%, `Cover Family` 90.0%→0.4%, `RB Align` 89.9%→0.0%.\n- **Same look + same call.** `form_fam_norm` × `run_concept` on early-down runs fragments completely — **0 of 67 cells clear n≥30 in both seasons**. The table ships with that stated, rather than a cell picked out of it.\n- **Whether the `pff_TEALIGNMENT` fill drop (54.4%→40.3%) is a mix shift or a charting change.** Excluded from the decomposition for that reason.\n- **Slot 2 of `offense_package`** (inferred FB).\n\n### 5. Lines for `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md` (I did not edit either)\n\nAdd under \"Things that will bite you\":\n\n```\n- **PFF `offense_package` is `WR-FB-RB-TE`** over the five non-OL, non-QB players\n  (`3-0-1-1` = 11 personnel). `(*)` = that many unplaced players, `(+Q)` = a second\n  QB in a skill slot, `X-X-X-X` = unidentified. Undocumented upstream; derived in\n  the Phase 4 spec §3. Prefer the chart's `Personnel` — 100% filled vs 97.8%.\n- **`mofo_coverage_played_shown` reads shown-then-played**, the reverse of its name.\n  Char 2 agrees with Baylor's 2024 `Cover Family` on 91.8% vs char 1's 67.1%. It is\n  ~97% filled on runs *and* passes, so it is the one cross-year defensive-look field\n  that escapes the dropbacks-only trap.\n- **Use `team_play.defense_package`, not the `rushing` feed's `def_package`.** It\n  covers passes too and agrees with the rushing feed on 100% of 819 overlapping rows.\n- **The chart's `Hash_O` is empty in both seasons.** PFF `ball_snapped_from` (L/C/R,\n  ~99% filled) is the hash.\n- **Alignment vocabularies drifted like `Play Type` did.** `Form Fam` writes\n  `UNBALANCED` in 2024 and `UNBAL` in 2025; `Personnel` goes from 4 labels to 11\n  (`12S`/`12B`/`12W`/`12M`/`12P`/`12J`). Normalise before any cross-year formation or\n  personnel cut, or a relabelling reads as a mix shift.\n- **Dead in 2025:** `RB Align` (89.9%→0.0%), `Front` (98.3%→0.0%), `Cover Family`\n  (90.0%→0.4%), `Front Adjust` (32.2%→9.5%), `Stunt` (collapsed to a bare `Y`).\n```\n\nAnd in \"How this project actually works\":\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python build_alignment_tables.py   # outputs/tables/alignment_*.csv\n.venv/bin/python build_alignment_report.py   # outputs/ALIGNMENT.md\n```\n\nAlso **correct the existing line** \"Current match rate is **99.3%**\" → **98.6%** (see item 6).\n\n### 6. Contradictions with Phase 1\n\n- **The match rate in `CLAUDE.md` and Phase 1 spec §6.0 is wrong.** Both say 99.3% and \"17 of 25 games matched 100%\". `outputs/GATES_PASSED.json` says `match_rate: 0.9855`, `perfect_games: 15`, and `outputs/REPORT.md` says 98.6% / 15 of 25. The report is right; the spec and CLAUDE.md are stale.\n- **Phase 1 treats a relabelling as two formations.** `outputs/tables/combined_formation.csv` and the report's Formation-family table list `UNBALANCED` (46 plays, 62.2%) and `UNBAL` (39, 56.4%) as separate families. Merged they are **85 plays at 59.5%**. Same defect in `combined_personnel.csv`: `12` (85) and `12S` (24) are separate; merged base-12 is **116 plays at 58.3%**. This is exactly the defect Phase 1 fixed for `Play Type` via `playtype_crosswalk.csv` and missed for formation and personnel.\n\n**Merge note:** if Phase 2 regenerates `outputs/joined_plays_enriched.parquet`, rerun both Phase 4 scripts — `test_chart_reattach_is_one_to_one_and_complete` pins 1,935 rows and will need the new count. Nothing was pushed, merged, or rebased; `phase4-alignment` is yours to merge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":551,"cache_read_input_tokens":259334,"output_tokens":3089,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":551},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3089,"cache_read_input_tokens":259334,"cache_creation_input_tokens":551,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":551,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ceu54JrCHA65upu2E1Cz2","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","at